# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. The drain records the tree's arrival with the barrier
# but lifts the read fence as soon as it has applied the rows: while the sibling's
# terminal is still on its own stream, this tree serves the saga post and the
# sibling pre. #4683's fix holds the fence until the barrier decides.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingCrossTreeImportLiftsFenceAtDrainEnd
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a cross-tree import notifies the barrier but lifts the tree's read fence at the end of the drain
PERTURBS: Bootstrap
BOUNDS: LossPath = 0, JoinStart = 1, SagaOutcome = 0, Shape = 1, PreHold = 0, DialFaults = 0

--- FIND
         /\ BarrierImport(snap)
         /\ outbox' = {r \in outbox : ~Aff(r)} \cup kept
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the fence is not held past the drain.
         /\ rout' = IF NotifiesBarrier(snap) THEN [rout EXCEPT !["A"] = ArrivalVerdict(snap)] ELSE rout
         /\ rstage' = IF NotifiesBarrier(snap) /\ rstage["A"] = "idle"
                      THEN [rstage EXCEPT !["A"] = "register"] ELSE rstage
         /\ afence' = afence
         /\ outbox' = {r \in outbox : ~Aff(r)} \cup kept
--- END
